Frostveil is derived from Vengeance (https://github.com/Grey-007/vengeance)
by Grey-007, which is also MIT licensed. The terminal/GTK file layout and the
general structure of this theme come from that project; the palette values, the
selection treatment and the border gradient were reworked for this theme.

The palette philosophy (a desaturated palette separated by a strictly
increasing lightness ramp rather than by hue) follows the design of the stock
Solitude theme (https://github.com/omarchy/solitude).

Neovim support targets ashen.nvim (https://github.com/ficcdaf/ashen.nvim), used
as a separate dependency and not redistributed as part of this theme.

The bundled wallpaper, backgrounds/BG2.webp, was generated with AI image tools
and is released under the same MIT license as the theme. It was veiled and
re-encoded for this theme but is otherwise unmodified in content.

Third-party components referenced by this theme remain under their own licenses
and are not distributed here.